---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';

// DRAFT (2026-11-24): not linked from the menu and marked noindex until Julian has reviewed the wording.
const doors = [
  {
    href: '#curious',
    eyebrow: 'Curious, not religious',
    title: 'Big questions, plain answers',
    text: 'Why do bad things happen? What happens when we die? Start with the question, not the doctrine.',
  },
  {
    href: '#christian',
    eyebrow: 'From a Christian background',
    title: 'What we share, and what is different',
    text: 'Same Jesus, same Bible. A few ideas are seen differently, and you can judge for yourself.',
  },
  {
    href: '/events/sunday-worship',
    eyebrow: 'Thinking of visiting',
    title: 'What a Sunday is like',
    text: 'Under an hour, a warm welcome, tea afterwards, and nothing expected of you.',
  },
];

const questions = [
  {
    q: 'Why do bad things happen?',
    a: 'We do not believe God sends suffering, or that everything happens "for a reason". People are free, and freedom has to include the freedom to choose badly. God never wants anyone to suffer, and is always at work bringing healing and growth out of even the worst things.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What about forgiveness?',
    a: 'We understand God as love itself, so forgiveness is not something we have to beg for. It is already there. What is left for us is the harder part: putting things right, letting go of resentment, and taking the next step.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when we die?',
    a: 'We believe life goes on. Death is a doorway into a spiritual world, where we are the same people with the same loves. Heaven is not a reward handed out or withheld. It is a way of life, built on love and usefulness, that people grow into.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is life for?',
    a: 'To grow in love, and to be useful to other people. We find that happiness tends to show up as a by-product of that, rather than something we can chase directly.',
  },
];

const shared = [
  'The Bible is God’s Word',
  'Jesus Christ is Lord',
  'The Ten Commandments, and the two great commandments: love God and love your neighbour',
  'Prayer, worship and a life that puts faith into practice',
  'Life after death',
];

const different = [
  {
    title: 'One God, not three persons',
    text: 'The Lord Jesus Christ is the one God. We see Father, Son and Holy Spirit as soul, body and activity of that one person, the way a person has all three.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The Bible has a deeper meaning',
    text: 'Alongside the stories as they are written, we read the Bible for an inner meaning about our own spiritual lives. Most of what you will hear on a Sunday is about that.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Salvation is a journey',
    text: 'Being "born again" is not one moment but a lifetime of change and growth. We also do not teach that the New Church is the only way to God. The Lord works through many churches.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Heaven and hell are chosen',
    text: 'God does not send anyone anywhere. People move towards the kind of life they have come to love. Heaven is open to everyone who loves God and tries to live by the Commandments.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Marriage can last for ever',
    text: 'Love in marriage is a gift that can grow deeper and carry on after death, when it is built on shared spiritual values.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is the New Church?"
  description="Why is it called new? The same Jesus and the same Bible, read for their deeper meaning. A plain-words introduction to the New Church."
  currentPath="/about"
  noindex
>
  <main class="container-prose px-6 md:px-8 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-16">
    <article class="prose-rnc">
      <div
        class="font-display font-semibold text-eyebrow tracking-eyebrow uppercase text-accent-primary mb-2.5 !mt-0"
      >
        ✦ What is the New Church?
      </div>
      <h1>The New Church, in plain words</h1>

      <p class="text-lg">
        The name sounds as though it means a brand-new religion. It doesn’t.
      </p>

      <h2>Why “new”?</h2>
      <p>
        The New Church is Christian. It follows the same Lord Jesus Christ and
        reads the same Bible as other churches. What is “new” is a fresh,
        deeper way of understanding the Scriptures, drawn from the writings of{' '}
        <strong>Emanuel Swedenborg</strong> (1688–1772), a Swedish scientist who
        turned to theology later in life.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name comes from the “new Jerusalem” in the book of Revelation,
        which Swedenborg understood as a picture of a renewed, more
        heart-centred Christianity. He wrote that he had been shown the Bible’s
        inner meaning. We don’t ask anyone to take that on his authority. We
        invite you to read, ask questions, and weigh it for yourself.
      </p>
    </article>

    <Card variant="tint" class="mt-8" eyebrow="Come as you are" title="What we don’t ask of you">
      <ul class="m-0 pl-5 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1.5 marker:text-accent-primary">
        <li>You don’t have to join anything, or sign anything.</li>
        <li>You don’t have to believe any of this to be welcome.</li>
        <li>Nobody will pass a plate. A freewill offering is entirely optional.</li>
        <li>Swedenborg is a teacher to learn from, not someone we worship.</li>
        <li>Questions, doubts and disagreement are part of the conversation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p slot="footer" class="m-0 text-sm text-text-muted">
        We are a small, friendly congregation. The Sydney Society of the New
        Church has met since 1875, and is part of a worldwide family of
        New Church communities.
      </p>
    </Card>

    <section class="mt-12" aria-label="Where would you like to start?">
      <h2 class="text-h2 mt-0 mb-5">Where would you like to start?</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          doors.map((d) => (
            <Card variant="default" interactive href={d.href} eyebrow={d.eyebrow} title={d.title}>
              <p class="m-0 text-sm text-text-muted">{d.text}</p>
            </Card>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="curious" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-24 prose-rnc">
      <h2>Big questions, plain answers</h2>
      <p>
        You don’t need any background in church or the Bible. These are a few of
        the questions people bring to us, and how the New Church tends to see
        them.
      </p>
      {
        questions.map((item) => (
          <>
            <h3>{item.q}</h3>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <section id="christian" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="prose-rnc">
        <h2 class="!mt-0">If you grew up in another Christian church</h2>
        <p>
          You will probably recognise most of what we say. The differences are
          mostly ones of emphasis. We aren’t asking you to leave anything behind,
          and we don’t claim to be better. Here is where we agree, and where we
          see things a little differently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Card variant="tint" class="mt-6" title="What we share">
        <ul class="m-0 pl-5 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1.5 marker:text-accent-primary">
          {shared.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </Card>

      <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-h3">Where we see things differently</h3>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        {
          different.map((d) => (
            <Card variant="default" title={d.title}>
              <p class="m-0 text-text-muted">{d.text}</p>
            </Card>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <div class="prose-rnc">
        <h2 class="!mt-0">Take it at your own pace</h2>
        <p>
          If you would like to read more first, the New Church in Australia has a
          plain-language guide to its
          <a href="https://newchurch.net.au/beliefs" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">core beliefs</a>, with a
          chatbot you can ask questions. When you feel like meeting people, you
          are welcome on a Sunday, and our minister is always glad to talk.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Button href="/events/sunday-worship">What a Sunday is like</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary" href="/events">What’s on</Button>
        <Button variant="ghost" href="/contact">Ask a question</Button>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
